## Alt text

Give every image an `alt` attribute. Write alt text for an image that carries information. Leave it empty, `alt=""`, when the image adds nothing the text around it does not already say.

| Image | Alt text |
| --- | --- |
| A floor plan or photograph that gives information | Describe what it shows that people need |
| A decorative picture | `alt=""` |
| An icon beside a visible label | `alt=""`, because the label already says it |
| An image inside a link, where the link text names the destination | `alt=""` |

[Images](../content/formatting-content/images.html) in the writing guide explains how to word alt text.

## Household identity images

A household name can be used on its own, with no image. If a household adds a crest or logo, keep its proportions and colours, and keep the name readable without it. [Personalise your home](../get-started/personalisation.html) explains how. The civica artwork belongs to [Project identity](brand.html).
